  "files": [
    {
      "section": "Clinical Analysis",
      "unlock": "Unlocked at 25 trust",
      "description": "Imaging tests reveal clear, normal outlines of internal organs, and no abnormal shadows have been detected. Originium granules have not been detected in the circulatory system and there is no sign of infection. At this time, this Operator is believed to be non-infected. \n\n[Cell-Originium Assimilation] 0% \nOperator Shirayuki showed no symptoms of Oripathy. \n\n[Blood Originium-Crystal Density] 0.12u/L \nOperator Shirayuki rarely comes into contact with Originium."
    },
    {
      "section": "Archive File 1",
      "unlock": "Unlocked at 25 trust",
      "description": "A reserved ninja who is incredibly succinct with her words, never using two when just one would do. \nYou never know where she might be until she is needed by the Doctor and she appears with unerring, possibly even eerie, dependability. \nHer hobby is apparently watching the snow from the coast, but it is not known if her preference is for the coast, the snow, or a necessary combination of the two."
    },
    {
      "section": "Archive File 2",
      "unlock": "Unlocked at 50 trust",
      "description": "Large shurikens are Shirayuki's weapon of choice. \nThere are many shapes and sizes of shurikens, but no matter the type, throwing weapons are always difficult to wield effectively.\nUndoubtedly, Shirayuki is an expert at using them, exhibiting accuracy and lethality that most normal people would find impossible given the unwieldiness of these weapons."
    },
    {
      "section": "Archive File 3",
      "unlock": "Unlocked at 100 trust",
      "description": "The ninja is commonly held as one of the national symbols of the Far East. \nThese mysterious assassins can allegedly walk on walls, burrow underground, and kill from impossible angles. They are said to value loyalty above all else. \nA ninja, upon pledging fealty, will serve his lord unwaveringly. And that is exactly what Dr. Kal'tsit is having an issue with--Shirayuki's loyalty lies with Madam Fumizuki, not the good Doctor at Rhodes Island."
    },
    {
      "section": "Archive File 4",
      "unlock": "Unlocked at 150 trust",
      "description": "Of course, the true purpose of Shirayuki's presence at Rhodes Island is not to protect the Doctor, that much is certain. That was just a pretext for Rhodes Island to accept her. \nStill, that does raise some questions. \nEven though it's ostensibly a partnership, Lungmen and Rhodes Island hold different views and objectives. Still, the Governor sent off his wife's personal bodyguard to protect the Doctor. Whether for surveillance or a show of power, it was very blunt, even unnecessary. \nSupposedly, Madam Fumizuki doesn't involve herself in politics, but it's hard to imagine she has no ulterior motive with this move. \nSo then, what are Shirayuki's orders after all?"
    },
    {
      "section": "Promotion Record",
      "unlock": "Unlocked at 200 trust",
      "description": "The princess said blind loyalty is nigh-impossible to find. But here you are, and I like it. —Shirayuki"
    }
  ]
}
